    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Sometimes the meeting point is described by a difference in distances. If trains move at 60 and 40 km/hr, then each hour the faster train travels 20 km more.\n\nIf it has travelled 100 km more at the meeting, they must have travelled for 100/20 = 5 hours.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Then total route length = (60 + 40) × 5 = 500 km.\n\nThe distance difference gives the time; the distance sum gives the whole route.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
