    "teach_6": {
      "id": "teach_6",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The after-meeting times can also recover the whole route if one speed is known. Suppose A:B = 3:2, so let speeds be 60 and 40 km/hr.\n\nAfter meeting, A takes 4 h to reach B: that remaining part is 60 × 4 = 240 km.\nB takes 9 h to reach A: the other part is 40 × 9 = 360 km.",
